{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Then I was</b> — אמון: from the sense of כאשר ישא האומן את היונק (as when the nurse carries the suckling), and it is a noun, and its form is like אמון, as in כאשר היתה באמנה, and it came in the manner of משחך אלהים אלהיך שמן ששון." "<b>And I was delights day by day</b> — it is possible to interpret it as 'and afterward I was delights,' and not while it was in the state of אמון." "<b>Delights</b> — a noun and not to be separated, like נעורים, זקונים. And it came in the place of an adjective, like והיה ברכה. And it is possible to interpret that a bet is missing, and it is as though בשעשועים יום יום, 'with delights, day by day, at all times.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The three scriptural citations here are fragmentary and their borders are unclear; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing. The last phrase appears to combine allusions to Psalms 45:8 and possibly other verses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:36.970938995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}